{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwfP1bbFh6M1vFCxCyDp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. After creation its status moved from pending to ok.\n\n**Data:** The data view `Kibana Sample Data Logs` (index `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`) holds web access logs. The fields I used:\n- **Request fields:** `response` (a string, so I used `response.keyword`), `extension`, `bytes`, `geo.src`/`geo.dest`, `clientip`, `url`, `machine.os` and `agent`.\n- **Response codes:** only 200 (12,832), 404 (801) and 503 (441) appear in the data.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-4445d318 Web logs overview\" has five panels:\n- Total requests (a single-number metric)\n- Requests over time (line)\n- Responses by status code (pie)\n- Top file extensions (bar)\n- Average bytes by source country (bar)\n\nURL: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-4445d318-web-logs-overview-5b3844da97fe\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-4445d318 5xx spike\" (id `b3c1dd21-e8cd-4999-9732-59eb1e2ac3df`) is an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute. It matches documents where `response.keyword` is `5*` and fires when the count over the last 5 minutes is above 10. It has no actions attached, so it records alerts in Kibana but doesn't notify anyone.\n\nI didn't check whether the dashboard panels render correctly, or whether the rule fires on the sample data."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":232,"cache_read_input_tokens":21383,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":232},"output_tokens":531,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"fa2feba3-4b3f-456f-a9ad-9dbc2b8